+## Publish-to-shared (#158 negative test, live)
+
+Step 4 instructs "Publish to `shared` — or record the exact refusal." The exact outcome is a
+silent scope hardcode, not a typed refusal. On disk at this base:
+
+- `coordination-store.mjs:14103` — `const scope = \`worker:${fields.workerId}\`;` inside
+  `writeScratchpad` hardcodes the write scope to the worker partition; there is no worker-visible
+  path to a `shared` scope.
+- `claude-session.mjs:103-118` — `scanForScratchpadWrite` admits only the closed shape
+  `{entry, expectedFence, idempotencyKey}` (`Object.keys(parsed).sort().join(',') !==
+  'entry,expectedFence,idempotencyKey'`); the up-channel wire frame carries NO scope field, so a
+  worker cannot name `shared`.
+- `coordination-store.mjs:14333` — the `shared` scope that exists is `settleWorkflowScratchpad`,
+  an orchestrator-only settlement path (`auth?.actor !== 'orchestrator'` refuses); not a write
+  lane.
+
+So there is no exact refusal string to record — a publish-to-shared is silently admitted and
+lands in `worker:<id>`, never `shared`. This is the #158 root cause, and it is still live
+because row-kernel has not landed. (Corroborates the lane-proof `lane-qa.md` L6 finding at the
+code level.)
